Subject: Close a class body at the end of the input with a MISSING semicolon

Close a class body at the end of the input with a MISSING semicolon.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
ff079a4.

93d3bcd closes each open block at the end of the input with a MISSING
`}`. The `}` of a class, a union, or an enumeration ends no declaration.
After that `}`, the state has no reduce action for the end of the input
or for one more `}`, and the sequence stopped. Error recovery then put
the full namespace into one ERROR node.

After such a `}`, ts_parser__insert_missing_braces now does the
reductions for a `;` lookahead and pushes a MISSING `;`. GCC reports
"expected ';' after class definition" (cp_parser_class_specifier in
gcc/cp/parser.cc), and Clang reports "expected ';' after struct"
(Parser::ParseClassSpecifier in clang/lib/Parse/ParseDeclCXX.cpp). A new
function does the reductions for one MISSING token, for the `}` and for
the `;`.

A MISSING token has the cost of a recovery. An ERROR node over a short
text has a lower cost than four MISSING tokens, and it stays. In a
namespace, a struct with six members and an unclosed function body gets
the MISSING tokens.

On the corpus at f8b702b, the files with an error stay at 17,242, and
the ERROR bytes go from 7,934,844 to 7,933,324. No file gets more ERROR
bytes. The tree hashes of the files with no error do not change. In the
benchmark of one error in each of 3,997 files, the ERROR bytes go from
1,984,250 to 1,665,132, and the named nodes outside the edit that change
go from 80,870 to 80,858. For the edits that remove a brace, the ERROR
bytes go from 1,327,970 to 1,064,510. `xtask fuzz --file-changes 256`
finds no failure in 2,188,519 changes. With AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, the incremental test of the files, the undo
test, and the test of the snippets give 0 differences.

The patch follows patch 08, and it has the same risk.

Risk for upstream: high.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

